## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to translate reliability risks into concrete actions, balancing external vendor risk with internal velocity, and creating observable gates and rituals.

## Key Concepts

- Reliability budgets and SLO/SLI definitions
- Backpressure and circuit breakers in distributed systems
- Chaos testing and staged rollout plans
- Incident management and post-incident reviews

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: calculate if burn rate exceeds budget
function burnRate(slo, breaches, windowHours){
  const budget = 1 - slo;
  const spend = breaches / windowHours;
  return spend / budget;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust SLOs if the partner outage lasts longer than a day?
- What dashboards and alerts would you use to prevent reactive firefighting?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates governance design capabilities for small remote teams, focusing on beginner-friendly processes that balance innovation with stability; emphasizes risk management, stakeholder communication, and scalable automation.

## Key Concepts
- Semantic versioning methodology
- Deprecation policy frameworks
- Automated compatibility testing
- Feature flag rollbacks
- Partner communication protocols

## Code Example
```javascript
// Version compatibility validator
function isCompatible(currentVersion, targetVersion) {
  const [cMA, cMi, cPa] = currentVersion.split('.').map(Number);
  const [tMA, tMi, tPa] = targetVersion.split('.').map(Number);

  // Major version changes are breaking
  if (cMA !== tMA) return false;

  // Minor version changes are backward compatible
  if (cMi > tMi) return false;

  return true;
}
```
